{"duration_api_ms":1782095,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b3582635-083d-4d21-a877-4ec6aedfc636","total_cost_usd":56.524361499999976,"usage":{"input_tokens":40,"cache_creation_input_tokens":29627,"cache_read_input_tokens":13653579,"output_tokens":13858,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2724},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":29627,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3192,"cache_read_input_tokens":695456,"cache_creation_input_tokens":843,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":843},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5[1m]":{"inputTokens":484,"outputTokens":172402,"thinkingTokens":53546,"cacheReadInputTokens":92338083,"cacheCreationInputTokens":604285,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":56.524361499999976,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":28,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Every item from the review is finished and the new 推荐 decision is in. `dart analyze lib test` exits 0 with the same 36 pre-existing info-level lints, and `flutter test` passes 98/98. The HEVC fix is checked with real ffmpeg. The Kotlin still hasn't been compiled or run; I checked it by reading only, so the picker and fd path need your CI build and a test on the phone.\n\n## What the killed turn left\nComparing against `snap2`: all 9 files the killed turn touched already held their complete, consistent edits. Only the test run and a `safeName` test were missing. This turn I ran the tests, added the `safeName` test, fixed one lint I had introduced in `flv_demux.dart`, and implemented the 推荐 change.\n\n## Review items (all done in the killed turn unless marked)\n- **HEVC switch through `hevc_mp4toannexb` (P2):** at each configuration switch, the first sample now carries the new VPS/SPS/PPS in-band, and those sample entries become `hev1` (the type that allows in-band parameter sets). A single configuration stays `hvc1` with nothing added.\n  - Verified with ffmpeg 8.1.2 on two x265 segments (640x360 then 320x240). Before the fix: 50 frames at 640x360 with `cu_qp_delta` errors. After: 25 frames at 640x360 plus 25 at 320x240, no errors. A switch back to the first configuration (A→B→A) also decodes correctly.\n- **Re-download deleting the only copy (P2):**\n  - A file that is only short (or missing) is resumed in place, which only appends.\n  - A structurally damaged file is re-fetched into `<seg>.redl` and swapped in only once complete.\n  - If segments are still damaged after that, the merge returns `damaged`. The entry is not marked complete, gets `failMerge`, and that is saved. The queue then waits, like a failed download, and restarting it fetches a fresh play URL.\n- **Repair fighting the download slot (P2):** repairs use their own per-video slot (`_repairManagers`). Deleting the entry cancels it; starting another download no longer touches it.\n- **Deleting an export wiping downloads in a shared folder (P2):** if the export's folder also holds download folders, only the export's own files are removed.\n- **Moving an old export aside fails silently (P3):** the move now catches the error (e.g. a file open on Windows) and carries on. The deletion guards keep the export and the download apart.\n- **OS clutter counted as \"foreign\" (P3):** dotfiles, `desktop.ini`, `Thumbs.db` and `ehthumbs.db` are ignored.\n- **`checkSegment` gaps (P3):** in strict mode, any bytes after the last complete FLV tag count as damage, and a `RangeError` counts as damage. Tests cover a cut tag header and a cut 64-bit box header.\n- **fd open failure leaves a black player (P3):** it now throws, so the player shows its error state. If `player.open` fails after the fd was opened, the fd is closed through a new `closeFd` channel method.\n- **Picker result lost on activity recreation (P3):** the pending result, the I/O thread and a main-thread handler now live in the companion object. On a real finish the pending picker call is answered with null and the I/O thread shut down.\n- **Persisted grants never used (P3):** removed `takePersistableUriPermission`, the 100-grant bookkeeping and the misleading comment.\n- **Side-file cache (P3):**\n  - Cache folders still shown by an open video page are kept, and released when that page closes (`LocalPlayer.release`). Folders no open page shows are removed on the next open.\n  - Copies go through `.part` and a rename, so a failed copy never leaves a truncated file.\n  - File names are sanitised: separators, `.` and `..` can't escape the cache folder. The `safeName` test was added this turn.\n  - Listing comment images is wrapped in try/catch.\n- **HEVC width/height 0 (P3):** the picture size is parsed from the SPS, including the conformance window. A test uses a real x265 SPS and gets 320x240.\n- **`video/*` hiding MKV (P3):** the picker uses `*/*` with a MIME list (video/*, Matroska, FLV, octet-stream). The provider's MIME type is returned, and Dart rejects anything that is neither a known video extension nor `video/*`.\n- **Two merges picking the same folder (P3):** the export folder is claimed before the first await, and released again if creating it fails.\n- **Not changed, per instructions:** the heartbeat (stays off for all offline and local playback), the rejected `firstOrNull` item, and force-adding the new test files.\n\n## New: 推荐 feed in login mode (this turn)\n- `LoginPolicy` now treats `recommendListApp`, `recommendListWeb`, `feedDislike` and `feedDislikeCancel` as account requests. They already resolve to the recommend-role account (`ApiType`).\n- The binding decision moved into a pure `LoginPolicy.bind`, which the interceptor now calls:\n  - Login mode on with a recommend-role account: the request carries that account.\n  - Recommend role anonymous: the request stays anonymous.\n  - Incognito: everything stays anonymous.\n- The access_key scrub only runs for unbound requests, so a request bound to the account keeps the key the interceptor adds.\n- Other home tabs (hot, live, rank…) are unchanged.\n- The doc comment at the top of `login_policy.dart` is updated.\n- `login_policy_test.dart` covers all three cases for each of the four endpoints, and checks that hot/live/rank stay anonymous. The two recommend endpoints moved out of its \"stays anonymous\" list.\n\n## Diff against `snap2`\n| File | Lines |\n|---|---|\n| `MainActivity.kt` | +61 −37 |\n| `download_service.dart` | +120 −36 |\n| `flv_demux.dart` | +94 −3 |\n| `mp4_remux.dart` | +79 −0 |\n| `local_player.dart` | +46 −14 |\n| `login_policy.dart` | +31 −2 |\n| `local_documents.dart` | +19 −1 |\n| `pl_player/controller.dart` | +18 −10 |\n| `account_mgr.dart` | +4 −6 |\n| `video/controller.dart` | +2 −0 |\n| `flv_demux_test.dart` | +90 |\n| `login_policy_test.dart` | +45 −2 |\n| `local_documents_test.dart` | +11 |\n\nI deleted my probe folder and scratch files; the three files left in `probes/` are yours.\n\n## Kotlin, checked by reading\n- The companion's private members are used from instance methods, which Kotlin allows. `pendingPick` now refers to the companion field everywhere.\n- `ParcelFileDescriptor.adoptFd(fd).close()` and `contentResolver.getType(uri)` are correct API use.\n- `EXTRA_MIME_TYPES` needs the `*/*` base type, which the intent now sets.\n- Copies write to `$to.part`, then `renameTo`, and the `.part` is deleted in `finally`.\n- The imports added are `Handler`, `Looper`, `ParcelFileDescriptor` and `ExecutorService`.\n\n## Uncertainties\n- **In-band parameter sets:** checked with software decode and ffmpeg's filter, not on MediaCodec itself. Only HEVC gets them. H.264 relies on `h264_mp4toannexb` handling the switch, which the auditor observed.\n- **Resuming a short segment:** if the CDN ignores the Range header and the transfer then fails, `DownloadManager` rewrites the file from 0, and bytes that were there can be lost. That behaviour predates this work.\n- **Closing the fd after `player.open` throws:** if mpv had already taken the fd before the throw, closing it could hit a reused descriptor number. I judge this unlikely.\n- **Recommend feed:** the app request keeps its per-launch `buvid` header even when bound to the account; personalisation comes from `access_key`.\n- **Cache folders:** one whose video page never opened stays until the next open or an app restart.\n\n```\nTEST RESULTS:\n  runner: flutter test (+ dart analyze lib test)\n  command: source \".../scratchpad/tools/local_env.sh\" && cd \"$REPO\" && dart analyze lib test && flutter test\n  exit_code: 0\n  total: 98\n  passed: 98\n  failed: 0\n  skipped: 0\n  duration_ms: ~315000 (format + analyze + test)\n\nINFRA REPAIRS (during auto-repair, empty if none):\n\nREAL FAILURES (audit-fix-caused regressions, empty if none):\n\nINFRA-PERSISTENT (failures that hit the 3-cycle repair cap, empty if none):\n\nOVERALL: PASS\n```\n\nThe Gmail, Google Calendar and Google Drive connectors still need authorizing in claude.ai connector settings, and `agentbridge` still fails to connect; none were needed here.","ttft_ms":12069,"type":"result","duration_ms":765293,"uuid":"80290fbe-3f5b-491b-ae3e-a6d223fc9334","ttft_stream_ms":11428,"time_to_request_ms":798,"first_content_frame_ms":11429,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
